  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Cole didn't last five innings against a team that came in fourth in the AL Central, and the Yankees couldn't climb out of the hole he left.",
    "what_this_means": "Detroit broke the game open in the third, scoring three runs before the bullpen even got warm. Blackburn and Yarbrough kept it from getting worse. Two scoreless innings combined. But the damage was done. Volpe and Goldschmidt both had two hits. The lineup managed seven total. None of it mattered because they went 0-for-4 with runners in scoring position. The Yankees scratched out two runs in the seventh when it was already lost. This is where the division margin gets thin: teams don't wait for late comebacks, and Detroit didn't let them close the gap.",
    "what_to_watch": "Casey Mize takes the ball tonight with a 2.58 ERA, and Carlos Rod\u00f3n. Who's posted a 3.13 mark over his last four starts. Has to be sharper than Cole was yesterday.",
